{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The credit type represents the appearance of the title, composer, arranger, lyricist, copyright, dedication,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and other text, symbols, and graphics that commonly appear on the first page of a score. The credit-words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"credit-symbol, and credit-image elements are similar to the words, symbol, and image elements for directions.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, since the credit is not part of a measure, the default-x and default-y attributes adjust the origin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the bottom left-hand corner of the page. The enclosure for credit-words and credit-symbol is none","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"by default."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLCredit"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, a series of credit-words and credit-symbol elements within a single credit element follow one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"another in sequence visually. Non-positional formatting attributes are carried over from the previous element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The page attribute for the credit element specifies the page number where the credit should appear. This is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer value that starts with 1 for the first page. Its value is 1 by default. Since credits occur before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"music, these page numbers do not refer to the page numbering specified by the print element’s page-number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The credit-type element indicates the purpose behind a credit. Multiple types of data may be combined in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single credit, so multiple elements may be used. Standard values include page number, title, subtitle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composer, arranger, lyricist, rights, and part name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<credit>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcredit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/init(id:kind:link:bookmark:content:page:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/bookmark","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/content-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/kind","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/link","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/page"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/Content-swift.enum"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"